
> smart-contracts@1.0.0 test
> hardhat test



  Account sensor session API and contract ledger (isolated sensor fixtures)
    ✔ Approve changes allowance only; Start and End produce exact stake/refund/reward transfers and visible ledger amounts (266ms)
    ✔ same-reference Start and repeated End are idempotent, and users/admin cannot End another user session (202ms)
    ✔ confirmed violation moves the existing stake to treasury without charging the wallet twice (184ms)
    ✔ SENSOR_FAULT returns the stake without reward (181ms)
    ✔ INCOMPLETE returns the stake without reward (175ms)
    ✔ the daily limit returns stake on a second valid session and the ledger shows zero additional reward (359ms)
    ✔ a pending signed stake survives recreation and resumes the same hash/nonce, followed by one real settlement (225ms)
    ✔ legacy orphan recovery refunds once without inventing sensor evidence or resetting chain history (122ms)
    ✔ an unavailable sensor rejects Start before any stake transaction is sent

  HRCRewardToken
    ✔ mints the fixed supply once and exposes no mint function
    ✔ supports standard ERC-20 transfer and allowance flows

  HRCSessionRewards policy
    ✔ exposes stable policy constants, outcome values, and addresses
    ✔ requires a two-coin stake and pays stake plus three-coin reward
    ✔ only an operator can submit outcome and client cannot provide amounts
    ✔ moves exactly the two-coin stake to the penalty treasury
    ✔ returns stake without reward or penalty for sensor fault and incomplete sessions
    ✔ settles a session only once
    ✔ pays only one reward per beneficiary per UTC day
    ✔ returns stake and reports an empty reward pool
    ✔ rejects invalid outcomes and preserves an unsettled session
    ✔ preview reports the same fixed policy before settlement
    ✔ supports operator-assisted session start for a beneficiary
    ✔ does not change total supply during pool, stake, reward, or penalty flows
    ✔ stores evidence and timestamp without changing policy amounts

  Ownership
    ✔ deployer is owner and operator
    ✔ two-step transfer: new owner must accept
    ✔ old owner loses owner rights after transfer
    ✔ only owner can start transfer; only pending owner can accept
    ✔ rejects zero address as new owner

  Operators
    ✔ owner adds operator and event is emitted
    ✔ rejects zero address operator
    ✔ non-owner cannot add or remove operator
    ✔ owner removes operator; removed operator cannot record
    ✔ cannot remove the owner from operators

  Recording safety events
    ✔ stores all fields and emits SafetyEventRecorded
    ✔ increases count and supports index lookup
    ✔ tracks per-device event count and last event time
    ✔ rejects duplicate event ID
    ✔ rejects invalid risk level
    ✔ rejects empty eventId, deviceId and zero hash
    ✔ unauthorized wallet cannot record
    ✔ operator can record
    ✔ reading a missing event reverts

  Automatic Emergency Stop
    ✔ DANGER locks the robot in the same transaction
    ✔ SAFE, LOW and WARNING do not lock the robot
    ✔ stores lock info (which event, who, when)
    ✔ second DANGER on a locked robot is recorded without a second stop
    ✔ locks are independent per device

  Manual Emergency Stop and Unlock
    ✔ operator can escalate a WARNING event
    ✔ rejects unknown event
    ✔ rejects event that belongs to another robot
    ✔ rejects events below WARNING
    ✔ rejects when robot is already locked
    ✔ non-operator cannot trigger emergency stop
    ✔ owner unlocks a locked robot
    ✔ unlocking a robot that is not locked reverts
    ✔ only owner can unlock (operator cannot)
    ✔ robot can be locked again after unlock

  Device identity and signatures
    ✔ owner registers a device
    ✔ register rejects non-owner, duplicate, empty id, zero address
    ✔ unsigned recording is refused for a registered device
    ✔ on-chain EIP-712 digest matches ethers TypedDataEncoder
    ✔ accepts a valid device signature relayed by an operator
    ✔ signed DANGER event also triggers automatic stop
    ✔ rejects a signature from the wrong key
    ✔ rejects tampered data (operator cannot change risk level)
    ✔ rejects replaying the same signed event
    ✔ rejects signature bound to a different contract/chain domain
    ✔ rejects malleable (high-s) signatures
    ✔ rejects signature with wrong length
    ✔ signed recording for an unregistered device is rejected
    ✔ revoked device can no longer submit events
    ✔ revoke rejects non-owner and unknown device


